# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Never commit .env.local, and never put a real
# secret in this file: it is committed on purpose, as documentation.

# ---- Database (required on Vercel, optional elsewhere) --------------------------
# Where the data lives. The same code runs against either kind of address.
#
#   A file on a school server, or on this laptop while developing (the default):
#     DATABASE_URL=file:./data/app.db
#
#   A hosted database on Vercel, which has no disk that survives between requests
#   (for example a free Turso database, in the Singapore region):
#     DATABASE_URL=libsql://your-database-your-org.turso.io
#     DATABASE_AUTH_TOKEN=paste-the-token-from-your-database-provider
#
# On Vercel, leaving DATABASE_URL unset is an error on purpose: a file: default
# would appear to work and then quietly lose every answer.
DATABASE_URL=file:./data/app.db
DATABASE_AUTH_TOKEN=

# ---- Admin panel ------------------------------------------------------------------
# You do NOT need to set anything here. The first time /admin is opened it asks you to
# choose a username and a password, and keeps them (as a hash) in the database. The
# password can be changed from the panel; if it is forgotten, `npm run admin:reset`
# brings the setup page back.
#
# A server that would rather set the admin itself can, with these three (optional). Do
# not write them by hand: `npm run admin:setup -- --write` asks for a password and saves
# all three here. When set, they win over a browser-made account. SESSION_SECRET signs the
# login cookies and must be at least 32 characters; without one the app makes its own.
#
# ADMIN_USERNAME=
# ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH=
# SESSION_SECRET=
#
# (The booth account for the kiosk and the TV is not here either: the admin sets it from
# the panel, and it is stored in the database.)

# ---- ระบาย (VENT) ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which AI answers students in /vent. While developing it defaults to `mock`, a template
# stand-in whose answers are labelled as a test. In production it defaults to `none`
# (VENT says "not available") until a real provider is added in lib/vent/provider.ts,
# so a template can never reach students. The provider's API key goes here too, on the
# server only. Choose a provider that neither keeps nor trains on what is sent.
#
# VENT_PROVIDER=mock
